\title{arraydesign: Acoustic Receiver Array Design and Track Simulation}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Places acoustic receivers on a depth raster, simulates animal tracks as a correlated random walk that stays in water, simulates tag transmissions with a random delay along the tracks, and simulates their detection by the array. Detection probabilities come from the detection-efficiency fields of 'detfield', so the simulated transmissions are heard under the model that will analyse the data the array collects. Scores a candidate array by positioning the simulated animals with 'detfield' and comparing the location surfaces with the true positions, and reports the share of the water the array covers.
